<title>SWEDEN: SAS, United sign freight pact.</title>
<headline>SAS, United sign freight pact.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scandinavian Airlines System (SAS) said it had entered into an interline freight agreement with United Airlines.</p>
<p>SAS said it would be able to offer broader coverage of ex-Scandinavia freight to the U.S. and United would be able to offer faster freighting to Scnadinavia via Frankfurt, London, Amsterdam and Paris.</p>
<p>The agreement also gives SAS increased freight capacity to Tokyo, SAS said. SAS freight flown to Beijing could be flown on to to Tokyo on United, which has a Beijing to Tokyo route.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
</text>
